# Bubble AI Test Report ✅

I tested both halves of the system end-to-end: the **FastAPI backend** (live server + real API calls) and the **Chrome extension** (real modules run in Node with mocked Chrome APIs + live AI calls).

## Test Results

**Backend — 34/34 pytest tests pass** (routing, fallback, memory compression, schemas, encryption) plus live verification:
- `POST /api/v1/chat` — Explain mode → answered via **OpenRouter**; Quiz mode → answered via **Gemini** (mode-based routing works)
- Conversations persist to SQLite (messages table verified)
- Server import gotcha: must run `uvicorn backend.main:app` from project root, not `cd backend && uvicorn main:app`

**Extension — 14/14 tests pass** (after fixes) covering prompts, ML classifier, memory budget, provider ordering, fallback chains, and live Groq/Gemini calls. Test script kept at `scratch/test-extension.mjs`.

## Bugs Found & Fixed (5)

| # | Bug | Fix |
|---|-----|-----|
| 1 | **Groq dead model** — `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` returns 404 on every extension call | Switched to `openai/gpt-oss-120b` (verified against Groq's live model list; matches backend) |
| 2 | **Gemini dead model** — `gemini-2.5-flash` is closed to new API keys (404) | Switched to `gemini-flash-latest` alias (matches backend) |
| 3 | **Mode classifier was silently dead** — TF-IDF seed corpus had no intent vocabulary, so "quiz me" vectorized to all-zeros → cosine sim 0 everywhere → always classified as `explain` | Added intent phrases to seed corpus + deterministic keyword hints (checked before embeddings) |
| 4 | **Retry storm on auth errors** — 401s were caught by the retry loop and retried with backoff (3 calls instead of 1) | Added `err.fatal` flag; non-retryable statuses now fail fast |
| 5 | **Test data polluted production DB** — `test_api.py` had written a fake `sk-test-secret` OpenAI key into `backend/data/bubble.db`, which masked the real env keys | Removed the stale row |

Also rebuilt `service-worker-bundle.js` from the fixed sources (backend tests re-verified green after all changes).

